how do you make a good first impression  with a potential investor or sponsor for  your business that's a question that  came in from one of our YouTube viewers  muzika who wrote in to say that I had  secured a meeting with a potential  sponsor for the business and wanted my  advice and what to say and what to do so  first of all Congrats that's a big jump  Congrats on reaching out and getting  somebody to say yes and agree to a  meeting huge step forward and hopefully  will help propel your business to the  next step in terms of what to say when  you get to that meeting a few tips that  will help you out number one understand  what they want so if they're sponsoring  your business I don't know what it is  that you do but if they're sponsoring  you they're after a certain outcome so  what is it  but if if it's some kind of charitable  event maybe they want exposure in the  community maybe they want some online  exposure maybe they want lots of people  to visit their website whatever it is  understanding what their goals are  there's probably a number of ways you  can help them out but you want to know  what their objectives are to start a lot  of entrepreneurs get that wrong a lot of  salespeople get that wrong they just  started to their pitch where the person  who's receiving it they're only seeing  one or two things not everything so you  want to try to target your message and  it comes from listening and  understanding what they're after  so start by asking questions get a  handle of why they're interested in you  then you could tailor your presentation  number two to show them a desired  outcome so now you know they want show  them how you can help them get it right  so if it's increasing visits to their  site increasing sales for them getting  more people following them on Twitter  whatever it is that their goal is you  want to show how you are going to be  able to help them if they sponsor you  the more tangible you can make it the  easier it's going to get them to say yes  and number three is tell stories stories  add a personal element to it it's great  to have facts and figures and to solve a  need but when you can add a story  whether it's your own personal story or  the story of another client who's gone  through it or some of that your help  as a result of them sponsoring your  event then that's gonna add a more  personal element to it and increase the  chances of them saying yes  so good luck listen to them understand  what it is that they're really looking  for target your presentation towards  them and show them the outcome and then  tell the story around it I know it's  really hard I remember when I was first  pitching my first angel ambassador for  my business I was scared  this guy had just sold his business for  700 million dollars and I wanted to get  a little bit of that to help fund my  business  and remember meeting him at a coffee  shop with my business partner and and  sweating bullets hoping that the  presentation would go WOW and we had  spent weeks preparing for this and we  got frustrated no we're sitting on the  couch day after day after day practicing  and wishing that we could have him for a  whole afternoon to walk him through  everything but you don't have that  luxury  now you've got to make an impact right  away you may have a maximum 20 minutes  with these guys and so you got to really  make that impact and let them know that  hey this is something they want to do  business with so practice your pitch  refine it down talk to yourself in the  mirror go over it again and again and  again the more practice you have the  better it's gonna be talk to your cat  talk to your dog practice in front of  somebody else so you get that feedback  as well and you get used to it even if  you're just presenting and your dogs in  front of you just getting used to having  somebody watch you even though it's not  another human being  helps prepare you so you're not as  nervous when you go into your  presentation so good luck keep us posted  I want to hear how how it went and if  you have any other questions let me know  those are you watching if you like the  video please give it a thumbs up below  what makes you want to do more videos  for you and if you have a question about  this video or question for your own  business I'd love to try to help if you  want leave it in the comments below I  always read those so thank you and I'll  see you on the next episode
 

